  "published": "2026-11-13T05:10:20.44Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Kazo OS 3.3.1, changes for app developers:\n- A window that comes to the front no longer reloads its frames. Windows keep their place in the page and only their stacking changes, so an app shown in a frame, such as Kazo Word or the browser, keeps its document or page when you click another window, and on mobile when you switch apps. A window that receives the keyboard focus, with Tab or a click in its frame, now comes to the front.\n- An installed app's page opens in its window, not a second Kazo OS. An installed app that shows one of its own web pages in a frame, such as Kazo Word, now gets that page, with the parameters in its address, online and offline. Before, the published Kazo OS answered with its own start page and a second Kazo OS started inside the window.\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/Os/releases/tag/v3.3.1",
